      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(localization): consolidate convergence and readiness",
        "body": "RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/42\r\n\r\nRelated: #88570, #107851, #106576\r\n\r\nFoundation series: 5 of 5.\r\nReview order: #111541 -> #111542 -> #111543 -> #111544 -> #111545.\r\nOriginal slices: giodl73-repo/openclaw#131, giodl73-repo/openclaw#132, and giodl73-repo/openclaw#133.\r\n\r\nThis draft targets `main`, so its GitHub diff is cumulative until foundation PRs 1-4 land. Its intended review boundary is signed commits `bf08fff1a64`, `7e12b541253`, `1a22ddf2245`, and `bdd0de1ca1c`.\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nCatalog presence alone can overstate localization maturity, especially for complex scripts, RTL interpolation, native quality, docs constraints, and pending human review. A product can report that Arabic or Thai exists while still containing English fallback pairs, unsafe bidirectional interpolation, stale native artifacts, unsupported docs, or translations that no accountable language owner reviewed.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nThis adds cross-surface locale convergence, simpler- and complex-script readiness evidence, zero Control UI fallback pairs, runtime RTL interpolation isolation, named-review manifests, and fail-closed final release readiness.\r\n\r\n## Main Interface And Design\r\n\r\nThe final evidence interface separates per-locale evidence from the product release claim:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\ntype LocaleReadinessEvidence = {\r\n  controlUi: { supported: boolean; fallbackCount: number };\r\n  cliOnboarding: { supported: boolean };\r\n  cli: { supported: boolean };\r\n  tui: { supported: boolean };\r\n  docs: { status: \"supported\" | \"platform-constrained\" | \"unsupported\" };\r\n  native: {\r\n    sharedArtifact: boolean;\r\n    androidArtifact: boolean;\r\n    appleArtifact: boolean;\r\n    qualityAdvisories: number;\r\n  };\r\n  review: { status: \"pending\" | \"reviewed\"; languageOwner?: string };\r\n};\r\n\r\nevaluateLocaleReadiness(evidence): LocaleReadinessState;\r\nevaluateLocalizationReleaseReadiness(manifest): LocalizationReleaseReadiness;\r\n```\r\n\r\n`LocaleReadinessState` emits an exact blocker union such as `control-ui-fallback`, `native-artifact-missing`, `native-quality-advisories`, `docs-platform-constrained`, or `human-review-pending`. `LocalizationReleaseReadiness.status` is restricted to `qualified-maturity-only`, `openclaw-owned-complete-with-platform-constraints`, or `fully-localized`. The generated artifacts are `simple-script-readiness.json`, `complex-script-readiness.json`, and `release-readiness.json`.\r\n\r\n`findLocalizationSurfaceConvergenceIssues` verifies that Control UI, native, Apple, Android, and docs projections match the shared registry and expected platform aliases. The generator publishes simpler-script, complex-script, and final release JSON artifacts. The catalog renderer additionally isolates interpolated literals with runtime FSI/PDI for RTL contexts while continuing to reject translator-authored bidi controls.\r\n\r\nThe generator consumes the complete ordered set of owner/domain surface\r\ndeclarations. Localization core validates the schema generically; the root\r\naggregator rejects duplicate surface IDs or order claims and preserves the\r\ncurrent 15-surface, 315-cell release portfolio. Gateway convergence uses the\r\ndescriptor registry shared from `packages/gateway-protocol`.\r\n\r\n## Example\r\n\r\nFor an Arabic approval failure containing request ID `abc123`, the translated sentence renders the literal as:\r\n\r\n```text\r\n... ⁨abc123⁩ ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe runtime inserts FSI/PDI isolation around the identifier so its left-to-right characters cannot reorder the surrounding right-to-left sentence. Translators cannot add arbitrary bidi controls to catalog source.\r\n\r\nEven with zero Control UI fallback pairs, Arabic remains below `complete` until its named review evidence matches the exact catalog revision. Persian and Thai docs remain disclosed platform constraints rather than being hidden behind a broad success flag.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nMaintainers get an honest product-level localization claim: incomplete, unreviewed, or platform-constrained cells remain visible and cannot be promoted to fully localized.\r\n\r\n## Final Exact-Head Proof\r\n\r\nAt `bdd0de1ca1c1bc6808fb366ef36ca0fa7cf0ed72`, all localization\r\nartifact gates pass and the full changed-test set passes 1,459 tests across 66\r\nfiles. The release report remains deliberately fail-closed:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nstatus: qualified-maturity-only\r\nlocales: 21\r\nsurfaces: 15\r\nfully-localized: false\r\nopenclaw-owned-complete: false\r\nblockers: 105\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis pass also caught and fixed one stale Control UI integration assertion:\r\nGerman now renders its complete approval-not-found translation, while a mocked\r\nmissing-key lookup still proves canonical server-English fallback. A fresh\r\n`codex review --base proof/main` completed with no actionable findings.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\nThe final five-bundle implementation includes readiness commits\r\n`bf08fff1a64` and `7e12b541253`, ownership follow-up `1a22ddf2245`, and\r\ntest-proof follow-up `bdd0de1ca1c`. Together they carry owner-published\r\ncoverage declarations, the shared Gateway descriptor boundary, changelog\r\ncleanup, and explicit complete-catalog versus missing-key fallback proof\r\nthrough the cumulative stack.\r\n",
